<td bordercolor="#FFFFFF" width="*" valign="top" bgcolor="#FFFFFF">
<h1>CORMAS: <b><font color="#FF6600">CO</font></b>mmon-pool <font
color="#FF6600">R</font>esources
and <font color="#FF6600">M</font>ulti-<font color="#FF6600">A</font>gent
<font color="#FF6600">S</font>imulations</h1>
<h5 align="right">&nbsp;</h5>
<h2>Welcome to Cormas ! </h2>
<p> </p>
<p><a target="_blank"> </a></p>
<p> </p>
<table style="width: 100%;" border="0">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="text-align: left; background-color: white; vertical-align: top; width: 435.583px;"><br>
<div><span><span>CORMAS</span> is an Agent-Based Modelling
(ABM) platform tailored preferentially to renewable
resource management. <br>
</span></div>
<div><span>Cormas is intended to facilitate the design of
ABM, as well as monitor and analyse simulations. It is
based on the VisualWorks programming environment which
enables the development of models in Smalltalk. Cormas
is a framework from which, by specialization and
refining, users can create specific entities for their
own model.<br>
</span></div>
<br>
- CORMAS is a free Open Source Software. Its last release
(02/2023) <a title="Download" href="en/outil/outil.htm" target="_blank">can
be <b>downloaded </b>here</a>. <br>
<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
<img src="images/newSimInterface.png" alt="CormasInterface"
title="CormasInterface"
style="width: 359px; height: 193px;"><br>
<address>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
The main interface of Cormas</address>
<br>
<br>
- On this site, you will also be able to access <a href="en/applica/applica.htm">application
</a><a href="en/applica/applica.htm">examples</a> (with a
models library) and <a href="en/bibliog/bibliog.htm">publications</a>.<br>
<br>
- We propose a <a href="https://www.commod.org/en">Companion-Modelling
approach (<b>ComMod</b>)</a> based on a computer tool, <br>
<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
<img src="images/applica/rehab-a.jpg" alt="rehab" title="rehab"
style="width: 387px; height: 197px;"><br>
<address>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
A ReHab session at IUCN 2021, with Cormas</address>
<address> </address>
</td>
<td style="vertical-align: top; background-color: white; width: 250.417px;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp; <a href="en/outil/outil.htm"><img
title="Cormas Logo Full"
style="width: 156px; height: 219px;"
alt="Cormas Logo Full "
src="images/CormasLogoFull.png"></a></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p><a target="_blank"> </a></p>
<h2>Training courses on modelling</h2>
<p>We&nbsp;are regularly delivering modelling <a target="_top" href="en/formati/formati.htm">training
courses.<span style="color: black;"><br>
</span></a></p>
<ul>
</ul>
<span style="color: black;"><img title="News" alt="News " src="images/new2.gif"
height="17"
width="31"
align="absbottom"><span
style="color: #0000ee;">
</span>International Summer School on ABM: <br>
<br>
</span>The <b>MissABMS 2023</b> session&nbsp; (<span style="color: black;"><span
style="font-style: italic;"><b
style="color: #ff2600;">M</b>ulti-platform
</span></span><span style="color: black;"><span style="font-style: italic;"><span
style="color: black;"><span
style="font-style: italic;"><b
style="color: #ff2600;">I</b></span></span></b>nternational
</span></span><span style="color: black;"><span style="font-style: italic;"><b><span
style="color: black;"><span
style="font-style: italic;"><b
style="color: #ff2600;">S</b></span></span></b>ummer
</span></span><span style="color: black;"><span style="font-style: italic;"><b><span
style="color: black;"><span
style="font-style: italic;"><b
style="color: #ff2600;">S</b></span></span></b>chool
on </span></span><span style="color: black;"><span style="font-style: italic;"><span
style="color: black;"><span
style="font-style: italic;"><b
style="color: #ff2600;">A</b></span></span>gent-</span></span><span
style="color: black;"><span
style="font-style: italic;"><span
style="color: black;"><span
style="font-style: italic;"><b
style="color: #ff2600;">B</b></span></span></b>ased
</span></span><span style="color: black;"><span style="font-style: italic;"><b><span
style="color: black;"><span
style="font-style: italic;"><b
style="color: #ff2600;">M</b></span></span></b>odeling
&amp; </span></span><span style="color: black;"><span style="font-style: italic;"><b><span
style="color: black;"><span
style="font-style: italic;"><b
style="color: #ff2600;">S</b></span></span></b>imulation</span></span>)
will take place<br>
<ul>
<li>from <i><b>September 11 to 22, 2023 </b></i>(2 weeks, in
classroom) in Montpellier, France at <a title="Agropolis International"
href="https://www.agropolis.fr/MISS-ABMS-2023"
target="_blank">Agropolis
International.</a> </li>
<li>By taking part in this course, you will gain a modelling
culture and learn the different skills required for building
agent-based models (ABMs) applied to sociological, ecological,
or socio-ecological systems.</li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li><b>Key points</b><br>
</li>
<ul>
<li>MISS-ABMS is multi-cultural in terms of background and
nationalities of the trainers and participants</li>
<li>MISS-ABMS promotes a collaborative practice of modelling and
simulation</li>
<li>MISS-ABMS is multi-platform: <a href="http://cormas.cirad.fr/indexeng.htm">Cormas</a>,
<a href="https://gama-platform.org">Gama</a> or <a href="https://ccl.northwestern.edu/netlogo/index.shtml">NetLogo</a>
can be choosen</li>
<li>MISS-ABMS presents the different stages of an ABM process,
with a focus on model design and implementation</li>
<li>MISS-ABMS offers a significant time for group work to design
and implement an ABM (see the <a href="pdf/leaflet-miss-abms-2021.pdf"
title="leaflet">leaflet</a>
or watch the <a href="https://vimeo.com/254868269">presentation
video</a>). </li>
</ul>
<li><b>For who</b><br>
</li>
<ul>
<li>Each year we enjoy having participants with very
heterogeneous profiles in terms of age, nationality,
scientific background and experience in modelling or coding.
Beginners in ABM who are planning to participate in a
modelling project in the months following the training are
welcomed.</li>
<li>If you have any concern regarding your participation, feel
free to ask at:<br>
<u>miss-abms_organizers[at]agropolis[dot]fr</u></li>
</ul>
<li><b>Information and registration</b><br>
</li>
<ul>
<li>For more details see the summer school website: <a href="https://www.agropolis.fr/MISS-ABMS-2023">https://www.agropolis.fr/MISS-ABMS-2023</a>&nbsp;
<br> </li>
<li>If you intend to participate, please complete the <a href="https://www.agropolis.fr/MISS-ABMS-APPLICATION-FORM">pre-registration
form</a> by <b>May 31st, 2023</b>. The selection of
participants and the confirmation of the session will be
announced mid-July.</li>
</ul>
</ul>
<ul>
<ul>
</ul>
</ul>
<ul>
<ul>
</ul>
</ul>
<h2>Last papers on Cormas</h2>
<ul>
<li><b><img title="News" alt="News " src="images/new2.gif" height="17"
width="31">
</b>A <a href="en/outil/classroom/index.html">new tutorial</a>
on tools for designing graphical interfaces is available.<br>
</li>
<li>Look at the video about our vision of "<a href="https://forum.comses.net/t/cormas-in-10-years/">Cormas
in 10 years</a>" during the COMSES 2018 conference: </li>
</ul>
<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <iframe
src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/dh9Eseu69fM"
allow="accelerometer; autoplay; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture"
allowfullscreen=""
height="286"
frameborder="0"
width="508"></iframe><br>
&nbsp;
<h2>Some references to cite Cormas</h2>
<ul>
<li>Bommel P., B&eacute;cu N., Le Page C., Bousquet F., 2015. <span style="font-weight: bold; font-style: italic;">Cormas,
an Agent-Based simulation platform for coupling human
decisions with computerized dynamics</span>. In, T. Kaneda, H.
Kanegae, Y. Toyoda, &amp; P. Rizzi (ï¿½d.), Simulation and Gaming
in the Network Society. Volume 9 of the series Translational
Systems Sciences pp 387-410. Springer Singapore.
DOI:10.1007/978-981-10-0575-6_27.&nbsp;&nbsp; Download the <a title="CormasforIsaga2015.pdf"
href="pdf/CormasforIsaga2015.pdf">preprint
version </a><a target="_blank"><img title="renvoi" alt="renvoi"
src="images/renvoi.gif"
height="15"
width="17"
border="0">
<br>
</a></li>
<ul>
<li>A translation of this paper <a href="pdf/cormas_ES.pdf">in
<span style="color: black;">Spanish</span></a> is also
available on HAL <a href="https://hal.archives-ouvertes.fr/hal-02156888"><img
style="width: 15px; height: 16px;"
alt="paper"
src="images/renvoi.gif"></a>
<br>
<i><b>Cormas, una plataforma multiagente para la modelizacio&#769;n
interactiva</b></i></li>
</ul>
</ul>
<ul>
<li>Check out the <a href="http://jasss.soc.surrey.ac.uk/15/1/10.html"
target="_blank">paper
on the Cormas user community</a> in the Journal of Artificial
Societies and Social Simulation.</li>
</ul>
<p><span></span></p>
<hr style="color: black;">
<p><span>This site, developed by the <a href="http://www.cirad.fr/ur/green">Green</a>
research unit (now called UMR <a href="http://umr-sens.fr">SENS</a>)
from <a href="http://www.cirad.fr">CIRAD</a>, is devoted to the
applied modelling of relationship between societies and their
environment.You will find here what we and our partners are
using ABM for the natural resources management.</span></p>
