    <title>Getting ready to use Cormas</title>
    <!--#include virtual="/include/script.inc" -->
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/cormas.css" --="">
    <style type="text/css">
<!--
.style1 {
	color: #FF0000;
	font-weight: bold;
}
.style11 {	color: #FF0000;
	font-weight: normal;
}
-->
</style> </head>
  <body border="0" onload="MM_preloadImages(/images/en/accueil_r.gif,/images/en/demarche_r.gif,/images/en/logiciel_r.gif,/images/en/applications_r.gif,/images/en/biblio_r.gif,/images/en/formation_r.gif,/images/en/reseaux_r.gif)"
    marginwidth="0"
    marginheight="0"
    leftmargin="0"
    topmargin="0"
    bgcolor="#FFFFFF">
    <!--#include virtual="haut.inc" -->
    <table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0">
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <!--#include virtual="sommair.inc" -->
          <td width="*" valign="top" bgcolor="#FFFFFF">
            <p><br>
            </p>
            <p> </p>
            <h1>Full installation of VW and Cormas</h1>
            <div>
              <div>
                <p>&nbsp;</p>
                <hr>
                <h3>1. Install VW7.6nc</h3>
                <p>Cormas has been developped for the <b><span class="style11"></span></b>7.6
                  non-commercial version of VisualWorks® (<em>Cincom Systems</em>).
                  VW must be installed on your computer. <span id="result_box"
                    lang="en">As
                    the 7.6 version of VW is not anymore available on Cincom web
                    site, and on the condition that you agree not to use Cormas
                    for commercial purposes, you can directly<a href="VW76.htm">
                      <b>download vw7.6nc</b></a> (version for Windows and for
                    Mac os X) from Cormas site. It is recommended to unzip the
                    archive directly under the <span class="style11">root</span>
                    of your hard drive to minimize configuration problems that
                    may arise with recalcitrant OS.</span></p>
                <h3>2. Install Cormas (VERSION : Cormas v.2023.02)</h3>
                <h5><span id="result_box7" lang="en">2a. Install Cormas</span>
                  for the first time</h5>
                <p>Download the latest version of Cormas (<a href="../../../logiciel/cormas2016_Full.zip"><strong></strong></a><a
                    href="../../../logiciel/cormas2023_Full.zip"><strong>cormas2023_Full.zip</strong></a>,
                  21 MB<span class="style1"></span>) of<span class="style11"><b>
                      February 2023</b></span>. Unzip this Cormas folder into
                  the directory VW7.6nc. The subdirectory cormas is created.
                  It already contains the<em><strong> cormas.im</strong></em>
                  file (instructions are detailed <a href="/pdf/installCormas2012.pdf">here</a>).
                  Copy your models in the subdirectory <span class="style11">VW7.6nc/cormas/Models/</span>.</p>
                <h5>(Keep your old version of Cormas<span id="result_box6" lang="en"></span><span
                    id="result_box6"
                    lang="en">.
                    <span style="font-weight: normal;">If an older version of
                      Cormas is already installed on your computer, you can keep
                      this version. Just change the directory name cormas to
                      cormas_Old or whatever.)</span></span> </h5>
                <h5><span lang="en"> or 2b. Update your Cormas previous version<br>
                  </span></h5>
                <p> If Cormas is already installed, do a simple update by
                  unzipping the <a href="../../../logiciel/cormas2023.zip"><strong>cormas2023.zip</strong></a><a
                    href="../../../logiciel/cormas2016.zip"><strong></strong></a>
                  (<span style="font-weight: bold;">2</span> MB) in <span class="style11">VW7.6nc/cormas/</span>
                  directory (erasing the previous cormas files). Open <em><strong>cormas.im</strong></em>
                  and select the menu: ? and Update Cormas.</p>
                <h5>or 2.c Alternative installation: from Store</h5>
                When VisualWorks is installed, download Cormas from the "Public
                Repository" of Store. From the VW main window, connect to Store
                (Menu -&gt; Store -&gt; Connect to Repository...), then
                select&nbsp; "Cincom Public Repository" and Connect. Thus, from
                Menu -&gt; Store -&gt; Published items, look for <span style="font-style: italic;">cormas</span>
                and load it.</div>
            </div>
            <!--#include virtual="/include/copyright_en.inc" --> </td>
          <td width="15" valign="top" bgcolor="#FFFFFF"> <br>
          </td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </body>
</html>
<html>

<head>

<meta name="KeyWords" content="Cormas, Cirad, gestion des ressources naturelles, natural resource management, INRM, environnement, environment, simulation, modelisation, modelling, SMA, MAS, multi-agent, smalltalk, visualworks, logiciel, software">

<title>Upgrading Cormas</title>

<meta http-equiv="Content-Type" content="text/html; charset=iso-8859-1">



<!--#include virtual="/include/script.inc" -->

<link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/cormas.css" -->

</head>

<body  marginwidth="0" marginheight="0" topmargin="0" leftmargin="0" border="0" onLoad="MM_preloadImages(/images/fr/accueil_r.gif,/images/fr/demarche_r.gif,/images/fr/logiciel_r.gif,/images/fr/applications_r.gif,/images/fr/biblio_r.gif,/images/fr/formation_r.gif,/images/fr/reseaux_r.gif)" bgcolor="#FFFFFF">

<!--#include virtual="../outil/haut.inc" -->

<table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0" width="100%">

<tr>

    <!--#include virtual="../outil/sommair.inc" -->
    <td width="*" valign="top" bgcolor="#FFFFFF"> <p>&nbsp; 
      <h1>Upgrading Cormas2004</h1>
      <p>&nbsp;</p>
      <p>If you have never installed Cormas in the VisualWorks environment, you 
        should go to the <a href="fullInstal.htm"> full install page</a>. Otherwise, 
        there should exist a <i>cormas2003.im</i> or (<i>cormas2004.im</i>) file 
        located in the directory Disk:\VW7\cormas of your computer. This means 
        that the configuration of VisualWorks should be ok. Then you simply need 
        to replace the kernel of Cormas that is incorporated into this image by 
        the new one proposed here. </p>
      <p>In the main Cormas menu, select <i>Help --&gt; aboutCormas</i>. If the 
        date that is displayed is prior to <font color="#FF0000"><b>december 4, 
        2006</b></font>, then you need to upgrade your Cormas.</p>
      <p> 2 possibilities to upgrade are available :</p>
      <ul>
        <li>from the <a href="parcelCormas.htm">cormas parcel</a> (the quickest 
          way) or</li>
        <li>from the <a href="kernelCormas.htm">new kernel</a> (the slowest way)</li>
      </ul>
      <p>This new version makes it possible to take snapshots and films of the 
        Cormas grid (this option requires <a href="http://www.apple.com/fr/quicktime/products/">QuickTime</a> 
        <a href="http://www.apple.com/fr/quicktime/products/"></a> and a DLL file 
        (<a href="../../logiciel/cormas2004/JunWinQT.dll">JunWinQT.dll</a>) to 
        be saved in Disk:\VW7.3\bin\win directory).</p>
      <p>&nbsp;</p>
      <!--#include virtual="/include/copyright_en.inc" --> <p> </td>

    <td width="15" valign="top" bgcolor="#FFFFFF"> 

    <div align="right" class="texte"></div>

    </td>

  </tr>

</table>

</body>

</html>

<html>
<head>
<meta name="KeyWords" content="Cormas, Cirad, gestion des ressources naturelles, natural resource management, INRM, environnement, environment, simulation, modelisation, modelling, SMA, MAS, multi-agent, smalltalk, visualworks, logiciel, software">
<title> Downloading Cormas2002- beta</title>
<meta http-equiv="Content-Type" content="text/html; charset=iso-8859-1">

<!--#include virtual="/include/script.inc" -->
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/cormas.css" -->
</head>
<body  marginwidth="0" marginheight="0" topmargin="0" leftmargin="0" border="0" onLoad="MM_preloadImages(/images/en/accueil_r.gif,/images/en/demarche_r.gif,/images/en/logiciel_r.gif,/images/en/applications_r.gif,/images/en/biblio_r.gif,/images/en/formation_r.gif,/images/en/reseaux_r.gif)" bgcolor="#FFFFFF">
<!--#include virtual="haut.inc" -->
<table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0" width="100%">
<tr>
    <!--#include virtual="sommair.inc" -->
    <td width="*" valign="top" bgcolor="#FFFFFF"> 
      <p>&nbsp; 
      <h1>Downloading Cormas2002 - beta</h1>
      <p>Many thanks to the beta-testers in advance.</p>
      <h2>The Cormas2002 new features </h2>
      <p> A short presentation (in french) : <a href="../../pdf/presentationCormas2002.ppt">presentationCormas2002.ppt</a>.</p>
      <p>The Cormas2002 version works with the most recent version of VisualWorks: 
        <b>VW5i.4</b>. <br>
        The new advantages of this version are consequently present in Cormas2002, 
        for example the NameSpaces definition, connectivity to all major relational 
        databases, object databases, and internet standard protocols. VisualWorks 
        is compatible with Windows&reg; (95/98/ME/NT/2000), PowerMac, Intel Linux, 
        AIX, SGI Irix, Compaq UNIX, HP-UX, and Solaris. </p>
      <p>Cormas2002 provides other new features such as</p>
      <ul>
        <li> the possibility to run a model without displaying the grid in order 
          to increase the simulation speed,</li>
        <li>the possibility of conducting sensitivity analysis more easily,</li>
        <li>Connections with Excel, allowing to save the data into Excel worksheets,</li>
        <li>Some facilities to build spatial aggregats, from regular or irregular 
          cells,</li>
        <li>Saving and loading aggregats with their components and their neighboors,</li>
        <li>the ability to works with different versions of a model,</li>
        <li>the &quot;pause&quot; button</li>
        <li>Cormas versionning </li>
        <li>an easier installation of Cormas2002 (CORMAS Parcel)</li>
      </ul>
      <p>The importation of your models from VW3 to VW5i.4 is dealt with by Cormas2002, 
        without munipulation of your code (normally!) </p>
      <p>Other features will be delivered progressively such as DB-connectivity, 
        GIS-connectivity, a movie make, landscapes indices, etc. A documentation 
        will be available soon, describing architecture of Cormas and explaining 
        a lot of methods.<br>
      </p>
      <h2>Installing Cormas2002</h2>
      <p>If you never install Cormas on VW5i.4, go on the <a href="fullInstal.htm">page 
        of complete installation</a>.</p>
      <p>If you have already install a previous version of Cormas2002 on VW5i.4, 
        just <a href="upgradeCormas.htm">upgrade to the current version</a>.</p>
      <!--#include virtual="/include/copyright_en.inc" -->
    </td>
    <td width="15" valign="top" bgcolor="#FFFFFF">
      <div align="right" class="texte"></div>
    </td>
  </tr>
</table>
</body>
</html>
<html>
<head>
<meta name="KeyWords" content="Cormas, Cirad, gestion des ressources naturelles, natural resource management, INRM, environnement, environment, simulation, modelisation, modelling, SMA, MAS, multi-agent, smalltalk, visualworks, logiciel, software">
<title>Upgrading Cormas Kernel</title>
<meta http-equiv="Content-Type" content="text/html; charset=iso-8859-1">

<!--#include virtual="/include/script.inc" -->
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/cormas.css" -->
</head>
<body  marginwidth="0" marginheight="0" topmargin="0" leftmargin="0" border="0" onLoad="MM_preloadImages(/images/en/accueil_r.gif,/images/en/demarche_r.gif,/images/en/logiciel_r.gif,/images/en/applications_r.gif,/images/en/biblio_r.gif,/images/en/formation_r.gif,/images/en/reseaux_r.gif)" bgcolor="#FFFFFF">
<!--#include virtual="haut.inc" -->
<table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0" width="100%">
<tr>
    <!--#include virtual="sommair.inc" -->
    <td width="*" valign="top" bgcolor="#FFFFFF"> <p>&nbsp;
      <h1>Upgrading Cormas Kernel</h1>
      <p>If you have never installed Cormas in the VisualWorks environment, you 
        should go to the <a href="fullInstal.htm"> full install page</a>.
      <p>Current version: <em>December, 2005</em></p>
      <h3>Loading a new Cormas Kernel</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Download the archive file <a href="../../logiciel/cormas2004/upgradeCormas.zip">upgradeCormas.zip</a> 
          (253 Kb) and unzip it into<br>
          Disk:\VW7.3\cormas\ (overwrite the existing files).</li>
      </ul>
      <ul>
        <li>Open <i>cormas.im</i><br>
          <br>
        </li>
        <li>Incorporate the new Cormas kernel 
          <ul>
            <li><i>Tools -&gt; Cormas -&gt; install Cormas</i> from the main VisaulWorks 
              menu porposed in the VisualLauncher window)</li>
            <li>select the file <em>Kernel-v.vendredi 2 d&eacute;cembre 2005 - 
              55140.st </em> located in the directory Disk:\VW7.3\cormas\kernel<br>
              (Be careful, this operation is rather long...)</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p><br>
        Thats all ! Do not forget to <b>save your image <i>Cormas2004.im</i></b> 
        (<i>File --&gt; SaveAs... </i>from the main VisualWorks menu porposed 
        in the VisualLauncher window).</p>
      <p>This new version makes it possible to take snapshots and films of the 
        Cormas grid (this option requires <a href="http://www.apple.com/fr/quicktime/products/">QuickTime</a> 
        <a href="http://www.apple.com/fr/quicktime/products/"></a> and a DLL file 
        (<a href="../../logiciel/cormas2004/JunWinQT.dll">JunWinQT.dll</a>) to 
        be saved in Disk:\VW7.3\bin\win directory). </p>
      <h1>&nbsp;</h1>
      <!--#include virtual="/include/copyright_en.inc" --> </td>
    <td width="15" valign="top" bgcolor="#FFFFFF"> 
    <div align="right" class="texte"></div>
    </td>
  </tr>
</table>
</body>
</html>
<html>
<head>
<meta name="KeyWords" content="Cormas, Cirad, gestion des ressources naturelles, natural resource management, INRM, environnement, environment, simulation, modelisation, modelling, SMA, MAS, multi-agent, smalltalk, visualworks, logiciel, software">
<title>FAQ</title>
<meta http-equiv="Content-Type" content="text/html; charset=iso-8859-1">

<!--#include virtual="/include/script.inc" -->
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/cormas.css" -->
</head>
<body  marginwidth="0" marginheight="0" topmargin="0" leftmargin="0" border="0" onLoad="MM_preloadImages(/images/en/accueil_r.gif,/images/en/demarche_r.gif,/images/en/logiciel_r.gif,/images/en/applications_r.gif,/images/en/biblio_r.gif,/images/en/formation_r.gif,/images/en/reseaux_r.gif)" bgcolor="#FFFFFF">
<!--#include virtual="haut.inc" --> 
<table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0" width="100%">
  <tr> <!--#include virtual="sommair.inc" --> 
    <td width="*" valign="top" bgcolor="#FFFFFF"> 
      <p>&nbsp; 
      <p> 
      <h1> Cormas Frequently Asked Questions</h1>
      <h2>&nbsp;</h2>
      <p>&nbsp; </p>
      <div align="center"> 
        <table width="100%" border="1">
          <tr bgcolor="#FF6633"> 
            <td width="16%"> 
              <div align="center"><font color="#000000"><b>Object</b></font></div>
            </td>
            <td width="30%"> 
              <div align="center"><font color="#000000"><b>Question</b></font></div>
            </td>
            <td width="54%"> 
              <div align="center"><font color="#000000"><b>Answer</b></font></div>
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr> 
            <td width="16%"> Cormas Installation</td>
            <td width="30%">Some trouble to make Cormas run under Windows</td>
            <td width="54%"> 
              <p>1. Copy the vw30 sub-directory of the CD on your hard disk (I 
                assume C:\).<br>
                2. Go into C:\vw30\Cormas and verify the properties of the cormas.im 
                and cormas.cha files (they should NOT be read-only !!! Please 
                uncheck the read-only button if necesseray).<br>
                3. Idem for the whole C:\vw30\Cormas\Models sub-directory (uncheck 
                "Read-Only" for all the files there) <br>
                4. Double-click on C:\vw30\Cormas\cormas.im. Windows then is requesting 
                the executable file to open this kind of *.im files. Click on 
                "Others" and browse to select the file visual.exe in the C:\vw30\bin 
                sub-directory.<br>
                5. Once VisualWorks is open, from the main VisualLauncher window, 
                in the "File" Menu, select "Set VisualWorks Home". Sometimes by 
                default it is set to C:\vw30\Cormas. It should be C:\vw30. Correct 
                it if necessary.</p>
              <p><a href="easyInstalOnWin.htm">Here</a> you can find an easier 
                way to install Cormas on Win.</p>
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td width="16%">Model installation</td>
            <td width="30%">Where should I save a model I have downloaded ?</td>
            <td width="54%">Often, the model you get, is a zip file. You must 
              unzip it into the directory VW3/cormas/Models.<br>
              A new directory with the same name as the model is created. It contains 
              the &quot;.st&quot; file and other subdirectories</td>
          </tr>
          <tr> 
            <td width="16%">point of view problem</td>
            <td width="30%"> 
              <p>When trying to change the pov, I have this kind of message: Unhandled 
                exception: Message not understood: #includesKey: UndefinedObject(Object)>>doesNotUnderstand: 
                Legend>>addLegend:location: Legend>>majLegendes: GrilleModele>>majPdv: 
                .....</p>
            </td>
            <td width="54%"> 
              <p><font color="#666666">Export and import your model...<br>
                For new pov to be taken into account in the legends, the two files 
                myModel.st and myModel.ev need to be analyzed, which is done when 
                importing a model... </font></p>
              <p>This bug has been <b>corrected</b>; see <a href="buglist.htm#legend">here</a></p>
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr> 
            <td width="16%">Programming points of view ?</td>
            <td width="30%">Can I program the choice of a points of view ?</td>
            <td width="54%"> 
              <p>Yes. It is necessary to give new value to the "activePov" attribute 
                of the metaclass Entity. For example, if you want to switch randomly 
                the pov on the cells every 5 steps, you must add the following 
                block in the step:t method of the XXX model :<br>
                <i>t \\ 5 = 0 ifTrue: [ XXX_Cell activePov: (Cormas selectRandomlyFrom: 
                XXX_Cell pdvDict keys).<br>
                </i><i><font color="#0000FF">"update the text of the grid bar" 
                </font><br>
                self space interface updateName. <br>
                <font color="#0000FF">"to force the display of all the cells" 
                </font><br>
                self theXXX_Cells do: [:c | c defineVisualState; show]]. </i></p>
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr> 
            <td width="16%">Programming the grid size ?</td>
            <td width="30%">Can I program the size of the grid ?</td>
            <td width="54%"> 
              <p>Yes, but just in the first instruction of the init method (just 
                after having opened the grid, if not the information contained 
                in the cells can be lost). For ex:<br>
                <i><b>init</b><br>
                self gridSizeCol: 50 line: 20. self initCells.</i> ... then add 
                the following method :<br>
                <i><b>gridSizeCol: nbOfCol line: nbOfLine</b><br>
                self space interface colonne value: nbOfCol. <br>
                self space interface ligne value: nbOfLine. <br>
                self space interface actionValideDimensionGrille</i><br>
              </p>
            </td>
          </tr>
        </table>
      </div>
      <h1>&nbsp;</h1>
      <!--#include virtual="/include/copyright_en.inc" --> </td>
    <td width="15" valign="top" bgcolor="#FFFFFF"> 
      <div align="right" class="texte"></div>
    </td>
  </tr>
</table>
</body>
</html>
<html>
<head>
<meta name="KeyWords" content="Cormas, Cirad, gestion des ressources naturelles, natural resource management, INRM, environnement, environment, simulation, modelisation, modelling, SMA, MAS, multi-agent, smalltalk, visualworks, logiciel, software">
<title>Upgrading Cormas Parcel</title>
<meta http-equiv="Content-Type" content="text/html; charset=iso-8859-1">

<!--#include virtual="/include/script.inc" -->
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/cormas.css" -->
</head>
<body  marginwidth="0" marginheight="0" topmargin="0" leftmargin="0" border="0" onLoad="MM_preloadImages(/images/en/accueil_r.gif,/images/en/demarche_r.gif,/images/en/logiciel_r.gif,/images/en/applications_r.gif,/images/en/biblio_r.gif,/images/en/formation_r.gif,/images/en/reseaux_r.gif)" bgcolor="#FFFFFF">
<!--#include virtual="haut.inc" -->
<table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0" width="100%">
<tr>
    <!--#include virtual="sommair.inc" -->
    <td width="*" valign="top" bgcolor="#FFFFFF"> <p>&nbsp; 
      <h1> Cormas Parcel</h1>
      <p>If you have never installed Cormas in the VisualWorks environment, you 
        should go to the <a href="fullInstal.htm"> full install page</a>. </p>
      <p>Current version: <em>December, 2005 <i><a href="../../logiciel/cormas2004/parcelCormas.zip"><img src="../../images/outil/parcel.jpg" width="16" height="14"> 
        parcelCormas.zip</a></i></em></p>
      <h3>Loading a new Cormas Parcel</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Download the archive file <a href="../../logiciel/cormas2004/parcelCormas.zip">parcelCormas.zip</a> 
          and unzip it into Disk:\VW7.3\cormas\ (overwrite the existing files: 
          cormas.pcl, cormas.pst and the &quot;Messages&quot; directory). </li>
      </ul>
      <ul>
        <li>Open <i>cormas.im</i><br>
        </li>
        <li>Close all windows (... except the main one : VisualLauncher, of course), 
        </li>
      </ul>
      <ul>
        <li> <i>Menu -&gt; Tools -&gt; Cormas -&gt; update Cormas</i><br>
          <img src="../../images/outil/updateCormas.jpg" width="546" height="326"> 
        </li>
        <li> If &quot;Update Cormas&quot; menu does not exist, please <a href="parcelCormas-old.htm">go 
          there</a>...</li>
      </ul>
      <ul>
        <li>Thats all ! Do not forget to <b>save your image <i>Cormas2004.im</i></b> 
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>This new version makes it possible to take snapshots and films of the 
        Cormas grid (this option requires <a href="http://www.apple.com/fr/quicktime/products/">QuickTime</a> 
        <a href="http://www.apple.com/fr/quicktime/products/"></a> and a DLL file 
        (<a href="../../logiciel/cormas2004/JunWinQT.dll">JunWinQT.dll</a>) to 
        be saved in Disk:\VW7.2\bin\win directory).</p>
      <!--#include virtual="/include/copyright_en.inc" --> </td>
    <td width="15" valign="top" bgcolor="#FFFFFF"> 
    <div align="right" class="texte"></div>
    </td>
  </tr>
</table>
</body>
</html>
<html>

<head>

<meta name="KeyWords" content="Cormas, Cirad, gestion des ressources naturelles, natural resource management, INRM, environnement, environment, simulation, modelisation, modelling, SMA, MAS, multi-agent, smalltalk, visualworks, logiciel, software">

<title> Downloading Cormas</title>

<meta http-equiv="Content-Type" content="text/html; charset=iso-8859-1">



<!--#include virtual="/include/script.inc" -->

<link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/cormas.css" -->

</head>

<body  marginwidth="0" marginheight="0" topmargin="0" leftmargin="0" border="0" onLoad="MM_preloadImages(/images/en/accueil_r.gif,/images/en/demarche_r.gif,/images/en/logiciel_r.gif,/images/en/applications_r.gif,/images/en/biblio_r.gif,/images/en/formation_r.gif,/images/en/reseaux_r.gif)" bgcolor="#FFFFFF">

<!--#include virtual="haut.inc" -->

<table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0" width="100%">

<tr>

    <!--#include virtual="sommair.inc" --> 

    <td width="*" valign="top" bgcolor="#FFFFFF"> 

      <p>&nbsp;

      <h1>Downloading Cormas</h1>

      <h2>Second step: Cormas users form </h2>

      <p>Before downloading, you are invited to fill the following form.</p>

      <p>Cormas authors would like to know who you are and the context within 

        which you intend using the software. No information you submit will be 

        distributed or used for commercial purposes.</p>

      <form method="post" action="mailto:cormas-webmaster@cirad.fr" name="Telechargement Cormas" enctype="text/plain">
        <p>&nbsp;</p>

      <table width="85%" border="0">

