<tr>

    <!--#include virtual="sommair.inc" --> 

    <td width="*" valign="top" bgcolor="#FFFFFF"> 

 <p><br> 
 <h1>Cormas overview </h1>
 <p>&nbsp;</p>
 <p>Cormas can be used to load and run existing models (some of them are available in the &quot;<a href="../../applica/applica.htm" target="_blank">Applications</a>&quot; section) and to design new models from scratch. The main interface is shown below </p>
 <p align="center"><img src="/images/outil/mainInterface.gif" alt="main interface" width="432" height="223"></p>
 <p>&nbsp;</p>
 <p>To design the current model, three succesive steps are suggested, as illustrated by the view on &quot;Program&quot; menu items below </p>
 <p align="center"><img src="/images/outil/model.gif" alt="main interface" width="582" height="362"></p>
 <p align="center">&nbsp;</p>
 <p align="left" class="texte">The graphical user interfaces involved to initialize and run a scenario are shown in the figure below</p>
 <p class="texte"><img src="/images/outil/simulation.gif" alt="main interface" width="686" height="352"> </p>
 <p align="left">Finally, the visualization tools allowing to follow whats happening during a simulation run are shown below </p>
 <p align="center"><img src="/images/outil/visualisation.gif" alt="main interface" width="473" height="299"></p>
 <p>&nbsp;</p>
 <p>To learn more about Cormas, try the tutorials provided in the <a href="/en/outil/classroom" target="_blank">virtual classroom</a>!</p>
 <table width="100%" border="0">
        <tr>
          <td width="33%"><font size="-6" color="#666666">Last update : June 
            03, 2008</font></td>
        </tr>
      </table>
