<!--#include virtual="haut.inc" -->
<table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0" width="100%">
<tr>
    <!--#include virtual="sommair.inc" --> 
    <td width="*" valign="top" bgcolor="#FFFFFF"> 
 <p>&nbsp;</p>
      <h1>Resources and Societies</h1>
      <p>&nbsp;</p>
      <p>Research on environment touches on natural resource and externality issues. 
        It deals with the management of renewable resources, the management of 
        production externalities (i.e. pollution) and the management of multiple-use 
        ecosystems. In all cases, the issue is to define and implement rules of 
        collective use.</p>
      <p>Both for the resources and the externalities, analysis must take into 
        account natural and social dynamics.</p>
      <p>The <b>natural dynamics</b> are characterized by the interaction of multiple 
        processes involving different species and resources, at different spatial 
        and temporal scales. · The <b>social processes</b> involve different actors 
        and several organizational levels ranging from individuals and user communities 
        to the large institutions that are responsible for development.</p>
      <p> <!--#include virtual="/include/copyright_en.inc" -->
	</td>
    <td width="15" valign="top" bgcolor="#FFFFFF"> 
      <div align="right" ></div>
    </td>
